                "type": "text",
                "text": "Read file /Users/charlie/Documents/Default Project/MEMORY.md, lines 1-490\n1: # MEMORY.md — persistent index for this codebase (no supermemory tool in\n2: session; this file is the store. Keep updated as the program moves.)\n3: \n4: ## Project\n5: spark-pipeline (`shadyuwugurl/spark-pipeline`, main-only, single author).\n6: Active program: Spark2.5-4B Darwin merges + hybrid layers + eval batteries.\n7: Prior programs in history: Forge/Nemotron CLI merges (deleted AGENTS.md),\n8: evo_spark6 scaffold (deleted from worktree, in HEAD). Unrelated dirs in\n9: repo: hermes-*, mc7-server-*, furarcher-asahi, memory-agent (Rust), chimera.\n10: \n11: ## Base specs (verified, do not re-derive)\n12: Spark2.5-4B: hidden 2560, intermediate 10240, 36L, 16 heads / 4 KV,\n13: head_dim 256, vocab 131072, sliding 512, 3:1 sliding/full, tied embed,\n14: 290 tensors, ~4.11B. 1.7B class: 2048/6656/28L/8+2 heads, 226 tensors.\n15: Merge anchor = stock `XHToken/Spark-X2.5-4B-Base` (cached). NEVER anchor on\n16: post-trained `XHToken/Spark-X2.5-4B` or an NSFW donor (lineage skew).\n17: \n18: ## Envs (load-bearing)\n19: - `.venv-darwin`: transformers==5.17.0, torch MPS, lm-eval, peft. ONLY env\n20:   that loads Spark2.5. System transformers 5.18 breaks (mask API\n21:   `inputs_embeds`/`cache_position`); 4.57 breaks (TokenizersBackend).\n22: - `.venv-mergekit` (mergekit-yaml binary works), `.venv-sft`.\n23: - No manifests, no CI, no branches (main only). Commits: `area: what`.\n24: \n25: ## Canonical code (why loads work at all)\n26: Muse `configuration_spark.py` (5.17 rope BC fix) + sriq `modeling_spark.py`\n27: + 2 mask shims + validator-clean rope_parameters (identical thetas).\n28: Built by `mk_workspaces.py` into `spark_merge_pool/ws/*` (weights\n29: symlinked from HF cache — never copy 8GB files). `darwin_merge.py`\n30: self-emits the bundle. No monkeypatches anywhere.\n31: \n32: ## Pipeline state\n33: - Donors cached in HF hub; 6 verified 290/290 (sriq, EP1, Muse, Heretic,\n34:   Japanese, Ocean). Pitcher fused (290T). 1.7B trio verified 226/226.\n35: - Outputs: 5way + 6way soups (HF, local = symlinks), 1.7B soup,\n36:   hybrid_spark_6way (434T, weights-only, no forward integration yet).\n37: - Eval: batteries 1-4 (lm-eval, MPS batch 8, `*,none` metric keys, f1/exact\n38:   + eqbench fallbacks). results JSONs are resume keys; back up before kills.\n39:   Battery1 done (6 donors): writing lineage leads hs/arc, mmlu flat.\n40:   Battery2 done (6 donors): same pattern; gpqa 0.28-0.35.\n41:   Battery3 (squad/emotion/eqbench) running. Battery4 staged (truthfulqa, bbh,\n42:   sciq, logiqa, aime24, mmlu_prox ja/ko/ru/zh, limit 50).\n43:   JUDGE harness rp_judge.py staged (RP/ERP/creative, adult-consensual only).\n44:   Master map: spark_merge_pool/BENCHMARKS.md.\n45: - Scores so far: writing lineage leads hellaswag/arc (~0.54/0.42); mmlu\n46:   flat ~0.674-0.683; gpqa 0.28-0.35; sriq squad F1 38, eq 16.4.\n47: \n48: ## Gotchas (paid for already)\n49: - `forge download` = metadata only; use `snapshot_download`.\n50: - lm-eval metric keys are `acc_norm,none` (0.0 defaults hid this once).\n51: - HF xet CAS errors are transient: retry resumes.\n52: - batch_size 1 on MPS = weeks; batch 8 = ~45min/model.\n53: - 8GB model loads: never stack two; sequence heavy jobs.\n54: - Server restarts kill background shells: relaunch + resume pattern.\n55: - OOM history: 131k-row embed chunking, MPS 256GiB blowup at batch>8.\n56: \n57: ## mlx-gablation (separate tool, `mlx-gablation/`)\n58: MLX-only behavioural-edit toolkit. NOT part of spark-pipeline; standalone pkg.\n59: Covers Gabliteration (arXiv 2512.18901, Guelmez), hedging/bias removal, doom-loop\n60: defaults, persona/corpus manifests, arch registry (lfm2/lfm2_moe/nemotron_h/\n61: spark2_5/llama/qwen2/qwen3/gemma). Env `.venv-gablation` (PEP-668: system pip\n62: fails). Test: `PYTHONPATH=mlx-gablation/src .venv-gablation/bin/python -m pytest\n63: mlx-gablation/tests/ -q` → 445. Venv uses `--system-site-packages` for mlx/mlx-lm.\n64: \n65: **Core invariant (do not re-derive):** an abliteration target is a projection\n66: whose output lands in the residual stream, i.e. `out_features == d`. Square\n67: (d,d) → `W(I-P)` right-mult; rectangular (d,ff) down-proj → `(I-P)W` left-mult.\n68: Right-mult cannot *read* a direction into a square matrix; left-mult cannot\n69: *write* one. Upstream FiditeNemini applies `W@P` to everything and hides the\n70: dimension mismatch behind a shape heuristic that is invalid for down-projs.\n71: Corollary: Spark2.5 attn `out_proj` is (4096,2560), NOT square (head_dim 256*16),\n72: so it is left-mult too. Only the right side collapses to Arditi `W(I-rrᵀ)`;\n73: the left side is `(I-rrᵀ)W` — different formula, two oracles in tests.\n74: \n75: **Verified on real weights:** LFM2.5-24B-A2B-MLX-4bit; 80 targets (38 moe_down\n76: banks + 30 conv_out + 10 attn_out + 2 ffn_down), d=2048. Quantized\n77: dequant→modify→requant confirmed; save→reload diff 6.0e-08.\n78: \n79: **THE estimator finding (do not re-derive):** the paper's SVD-of-paired-difference\n80: extractor is variance-dominated at bank sizes we can afford. Measured with a\n81: corrected harness (control bank must read SIGNAL or the harness is broken):\n82: control excess +0.38→+0.73, xstest excess +0.208 (n=8) decaying to +0.029 (n=28)\n83: for SVD, but +0.548→+0.759 for Arditi mean_difference. The pipeline was ablating\n84: a *noise* direction, which is why refusal went UP 0.467→0.733. **Use\n85: `--method mean_diff`; keep `gabliteration` as the paper-faithful path for\n86: 10k-prompt banks.** Four of my own hypotheses died on measurement (depth-biased\n87: `norm`; unpaired banks; probe position; outlier dims) — the harness was buggy\n88: each time, so always run the positive control first.\n89: \n90: **Coverage beats strength** (sweep on Qwen3-1.7B, xstest, mean_diff):\n91: a0.3_L3 harmful −0.025 · a1.0_L3 +0.000 · **a1.0_L12 −0.100** · a2.0_L16 +0.188\n92: AND over-refusal +0.300 (catastrophic). α alone is not monotone; editing 3\n93: layers is too small to matter, editing 12 at α=1.0 works, α=2.0 breaks the\n94: model. Capability stayed 1.000 in every config.\n95: \n96: **Methodology rules the repo enforces (each was a real bug):** (1) disjoint\n97: extraction/eval splits; (2) TWO-SIDED scoring — a refusal rate alone measures\n98: nothing, since a model that never refuses scores 0.000 while being useless;\n99: `benchmarks.compare` refuses to call a change an improvement if over-refusal\n100: rises; (3) chat template applied (`mlx_lm.generate` does not apply one);\n101: (4) positive control must read SIGNAL or the result is void.\n102: **Never evaluate on a subset selected by the metric being reported** — that\n103: inflates results (measured: 0.500→0.000 on a refusing subset vs 0.000→0.000\n104: on the full bank).\n105: \n106: **Bugs that only real weights found:** (1) `_weight_shape` checked `scales`\n107: before `weight.ndim`, so *quantized* 3-D MoE banks got in_features = out*group_size\n108: = 131072 and were silently filtered out — 42→80 targets once the ndim branch goes\n109: first; synthetic unquantized fixtures missed it entirely. (2) MLX float32\n110: matmuls on this M5 are only ~1e-3 accurate (Metal reduced-precision path), so\n111: float32 surgery leaves 7.7e-4 of the direction; float64 CPU leaves 2.6e-8.\n112: Use `--precision float64`. (3) mlx_lm `generate` applies NO chat template and\n113: returns `str` not `.text`; no `sampler_args`; repetition penalty is a logits\n114: processor. (4) `mlx.nn` has NO `QuantizedSwitchLinear` — the class lives in\n115: `mlx_lm.models.switch_layers` and is NOT an `nn.QuantizedLinear`, so an\n116: `isinstance` check silently treated packed uint32 expert weights as dense\n117: float and DESTROYED the bank (max|dW| 5.6e9, run still reported success).\n118: Duck-type on `.scales`/`.group_size`/`.bits` instead. (5) LFM2.5-24B's chat\n119: template opens `<think>` UNCONDITIONALLY (no enable_thinking toggle) and the\n120: model reasons for 100s of tokens: at a 96-token budget 5 of 6 harmful\n121: completions never left the think block, so the answer-style refusal markers\n122: never saw the refusal and the baseline read 0.084 for a model that refuses on\n123: essentially every one. Fixed by `REFUSAL_DECISION_PATTERNS` (refusal\n124: decisions as reasoning prose states them, every pattern negation-aware so a\n125: benign \"this is not disallowed\" is not scored) + `refusal_rate(thinking=True)`\n126: reporting rate / answer_rate / truncated_rate. A template containing `<think>`\n127: is NOT the same as a model that thinks — Qwen3 accepts enable_thinking=False,\n128: LFM2.5 does not; `decisive.py` asks the runner, not the template.\n129: \n130: **MLX 0.32 optimizer landmine:** `mlx.optimizers.MultiOptimizer.apply_gradients`\n131: hands each sub-optimizer the SPLIT gradient tree but the FULL parameter tree,\n132: so a filtered split dies with `IndexError: list index out of range` in\n133: `update_state`. `scripts/train_lora.py` has its own `SplitOptimizer` that\n134: splits gradients AND parameters and skips empty groups (`Optimizer.init` on an\n135: empty parameter list indexes `params[0]` against its `{\"step\":...}` state and\n136: crashes). Also: `model.freeze()` must come BEFORE `linear_to_lora_layers`\n137: (otherwise the whole model is trainable), `ChatDataset` must be wrapped in\n138: `CacheDataset` (else the trainer raises `KeyError: 0`), `nn.value_and_grad`\n139: returns a function you must call, and `mlx.utils.tree_flatten` returns a LIST\n140: of (dotted_key, array) pairs.\n141: \n142: **MoE surgery needs chunking:** a 64-expert (64, 2048, 1536) bank is 805 MB\n143: in float32 and the surgery needs several copies live at once, so editing 24\n144: such banks in one pass needs ~19 GB on top of the 12 GB 4-bit model and dies\n145: with Metal \"Insufficient Memory\" partway through the after-half (which reads\n146: as a result if you are not watching the log). `apply_to_targets` now edits\n147: banks a slice of experts at a time (`--expert-chunk`, default 8); the chunk\n148: size changes peak memory, not the result (a test asserts chunked ==\n149: unchunked to 1e-6). Never run the 24B concurrently with anything else.\n150: \n151: **A direction that only moves its own fitting set is not a behaviour\n152: removal.** Three hedging banks, three results: the content-elicited one\n153: reverses (+0.167 hedge, a genre axis); the topic- and form-balanced one works\n154: on its own fitting set (-0.100) but reverses on unseen questions (+0.083) and\n155: the reverse direction does nothing (+0.000). Refusal is the contrast that\n156: makes it legible: the matched-bank direction did move the *disjoint* eval\n157: split (0.537 -> 0.487). Always score a direction on a bank it was not\n158: fitted on.\n159: \n160: **Bank pairing is load-bearing (end-to-end, not just stability):** with the\n161: same estimator, strength and eval suite, a MATCHED minimal-contrast bank gave\n162: harmful −0.100 (PASS) and a WILDCARD bank (wildjailbreak) gave +0.100\n163: (FAIL, reversed). wildjailbreak's \"harmful\" bucket contains innocuous prompts\n164: and its \"benign\" bucket whimsical ones, so the mean difference captures a\n165: topic axis, not a safety axis.\n166: \n167: **Toxicity is a double-gate** (`persona.assemble_corpus`): needs BOTH\n168: `toxicity_corpus=<hf id>` AND `allow_toxicity=True`, no defaults, no preset.\n169: \n170: **t4-1 additions — heretic-style global direction + J-Wash wash (do not re-derive):**\n171: `--method global_svd` is the heretic estimator, reimplemented clean-room (heretic\n172: is AGPL-3.0, so no code was copied): the per-layer difference matrices are\n173: stacked into one (N,d) matrix and the top right singular vectors of that stack\n174: become ONE direction used by every edited layer. It CANNOT live in\n175: `directions.EXTRACTORS` — those receive a single layer's activations, this needs\n176: all of them — so `pipeline.gabliterate` special-cases it and `DirectionSet.layer`\n177: is set to `pipeline.GLOBAL_LAYER = -1` (\"belongs to no single layer\"). The sign of\n178: an SVD vector is arbitrary, so it is fixed by aligning with the pooled mean\n179: difference (the positive side must project higher, else the edit reinforces the\n180: behaviour instead of removing it). `directions.stacked_differences` does the\n181: pairing — rows are paired positionally, because the capture runs the same\n182: prompts on both sides.\n183: `--wash {plain,orthogonalize,jwash}` is the J-Wash recipe (Apache-2.0, attribute\n184: in the PR body): `orthogonalize` restores the edited matrix's ORIGINAL singular\n185: values while keeping its own singular vectors, so the behaviour direction really\n186: is written into the weights but the layer's output scale does not move;\n187: `jwash` = orthogonalize + rescale the Frobenius norm to the original.\n188: `surgery.restore_singular_values` / `rescale_frobenius` do the work in numpy\n189: float64 (MLX float32 matmuls on this M5 are ~1e-3 accurate) and accept a single\n190: matrix (m,n) or an expert stack (E,m,n). `surgery._postprocess_weight` is the\n191: mx-array wrapper, called from `apply_to_targets` in BOTH the dense branch and the\n192: expert branch. `pipeline._wash_steps` maps a wash name to (orthogonalize, rescale).\n193: \n194: ## t4-2 additions (do not re-derive)\n195: \n196: **Per-layer directions (ZeroFuse-shaped, MIT source read only).**\n197: `directions.per_layer_directions(pos_states, neg_states, layers=None, k=1,\n198: method=\"mean_diff\")` → `{layer: (d,k)}`; it loops the per-layer extractors over\n199: the layers BOTH banks were captured for, and the rows stay aligned because the\n200: capture runs the same prompts on both sides. `directions.fuse_directions(bases,\n201: weights=None)` → `(d,r)`: stacks the per-layer bases as ROWS, takes the top\n202: right singular vectors of that stack, keeps `n_cols` columns, and fixes the\n203: sign by aligning with the summed per-basis means (falling back to the FIRST\n204: basis' mean when the inputs cancel, so the sign is never the arbitrary one of\n205: a singular vector). `directions.fractional_layer_index(frac, n_layers)` maps a\n206: fractional depth to a layer (0.0 → first block, 1.0 → last).\n207: \n208: **Wiring constraint.** The `EXTRACTORS` registry is per-layer\n209: `(H_pos, H_neg) -> (d,k)`, so a method that needs every layer CANNOT be an\n210: EXTRACTORS entry. `global_svd`, `per_layer` and `fused` are special-cased in\n211: `pipeline.gabliterate` Phase 2 instead; `extractor_layer` is set to\n212: `GLOBAL_LAYER` (-1) for `global_svd`. In the `per_layer` mode the\n213: `DirectionSet` carries the FUSED basis for provenance while the per-layer\n214: bases drive the edit. `surgery.apply_to_targets` takes a `projector_for(target)`\n215: resolver: one `Projector` (unchanged), a dict `{layer: Projector}`, or a\n216: callable. The embedding falls back to the shared projector.\n217: \n218: **The embedding role (Auto-Abliteration-shaped).** The token embedding is a\n219: SOURCE of residual vectors, not a write into them, so it is not a\n220: residual-write projection: `arch.EMBED_LAYER = -2` (distinct from\n221: `GLOBAL_LAYER = -1`), `arch._embedding_target` gives it `side=\"right\"` (each\n222: row is a token's residual vector, so the direction is read out of E's COLUMNS —\n223: the opposite side from a down-projection, which is left-multiplied), and\n224: `resolve_targets` detects it BEFORE the `_excluded_prefix` and\n225: `layer is None` skips. **`\"embed\"` is deliberately NOT in `arch.ALL_ROLES`** —\n226: it is opt-in via `--embed` / `roles=(\"embed\",)`, so the default target set is\n227: unchanged. The embedding belongs to no block, so it gets its own alpha\n228: (`--embed-alpha`, defaulting to the first edited block's).\n229: \n230: **The tuner (abliterix-shaped, AGPL source read only).** The package ALREADY\n231: had `tune.py` (`TuneCandidate`, `TuneMeasurement`, `TuneResult`, `TuneReport`,\n232: `candidate_grid`, `composite_score`, `search`, `tune_model`,\n233: `make_generate_fn`) — do NOT add a second tuner. `composite_score` =\n234: `refusal + lam*over_refusal + mu*fidelity` (smaller is better); `search` is\n235: pure and model-free, and a candidate whose measurement raises is recorded in\n236: `report.failures` instead of aborting the sweep. `tune_model` snapshots the\n237: weights, restores them before every candidate, and restores them again in a\n238: `finally:` block.\n239: \n240: Two guards were added to `tune.py`:\n241: * `tune.kl_divergence(ref, mod, floor=1e-9)` — KL over two aligned lists of\n242:   top-k log-probability dicts, each side renormalised over its own top-k\n243:   (the tables are truncated, so their masses do not sum to one). It accepts\n244:   probability tables too: a table is treated as log-probs when it holds a\n245:   negative entry. `tune._topk_logprobs(model, tokenizer, prompts, k=20)` reads\n246:   the last position and swallows per-prompt exceptions.\n247: * `tune.control_verdict(base_rate, candidate_rates, tolerance=0.0)` — the\n248:   POSITIVE CONTROL. If no candidate moved the refusal metric, the harness is\n249:   not reading signal and the ranking is meaningless, so it returns False and\n250:   the sweep must not crown a winner. `mlx-gablate tune` prints the control\n251:   verdict and exits 2 when it fails.\n252: \n253: **The drift audit (abldrift-shaped, MIT).** `drift.py` is new: `Probe`,\n254: `DeltaVector`, `bootstrap_ci` (percentile bootstrap of the mean),\n255: `compute_delta` (paired `modified - base`), `load_probes` (JSON or YAML),\n256: `lexical_judge` (cue hits per 100 words), `paired_audit`, `compare_audits`,\n257: `default_probes`, `format_report`. A dimension counts as drifted only when the\n258: mean moved AND the bootstrap interval excludes zero — a shift within the noise\n259: is not a finding. `mlx-gablate drift --model M --baseline B` runs the same\n260: probes against both models and exits 1 when something breached.\n261: \n262: **New CLI commands:** `mlx-gablate tune` (search (method, layers, alpha) with\n263: the control check) and `mlx-gablate drift` (paired before/after character\n264: audit). `mlx-gablate gabliterate` gained `--embed`, `--embed-alpha`,\n265: `--base-method` and `--layer-frac`; `--method` gained `per_layer` and `fused`.\n266: \n267: ## t4-3 / t4-4 findings (do not re-derive)\n268: \n269: - **`io.load_model` returns `(model, config)`, not `(model, tokenizer)`.** It wraps\n270:   `mlx_lm.utils.load_model`. Anything that needs a tokenizer has to build one:\n271:   `AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(str(path), trust_remote_code=...)`. Passing the\n272:   config dict as the tokenizer fails deep inside `mlx_lm.generate` with\n273:   `AttributeError: 'dict' object has no attribute 'decode'`.\n274: - **`mlx_lm.generate` has no `temperature` kwarg.** On mlx-lm 0.32.0\n275:   `stream_generate` forwards `**kwargs` to `generate_step`, which accepts a\n276:   prebuilt `sampler` and `logits_processors` only, so `temperature=` raises\n277:   `TypeError: generate_step() got an unexpected keyword argument 'temperature'`.\n278:   Use `loops.mlx_sampling_kwargs({\"temp\": t, \"top_p\": p}, None, tokenizer)`.\n279: - **`cli.py`'s `bench` command is broken today**: `_cmd_bench` calls\n280:   `_load_tokenizer(args.model)` and no `_load_tokenizer` is defined anywhere in\n281:   the package, so it raises `NameError`. Unfixed as of t4-3.\n282: - **`.venv-gablation` resolves mlx-lm 0.32.0** through the homebrew system\n283:   site-packages (python 3.14), not 0.32.2.\n284: - **t4-3 dispositions** (full write-up in `mlx-lab/docs/P4_CLUSTER.md`):\n285:   KVarN is a vLLM/CUDA KV-cache quantisation *inference* backend, so it\n286:   belongs to the inference/cache phase and not to the weight-edit toolkit;\n287:   HALOs is a PyTorch alignment-loss library, but it exposes the real gap that\n288:   **mlx-lm-lora has no KTO trainer** (no `kto_trainer.py`, no `kto` in\n289:   `train.py`'s `train_mode` dispatch, no `kto` in the Studio's `PIPELINES`);\n290:   senbonzakura's distinctive contribution is measuring what the edit cost, which\n291:   `benchmarks.py` already does.\n292: \n293: ## Unsloth Studio (local, controllable — see `docs/unsloth-studio-control.md`)\n294: Running at `http://127.0.0.1:8888` (REST) and `http://127.0.0.1:8888/mcp/`\n295: (MCP), key `sk-unsloth-559b6cfa3d5e7e231d73d6dcf1dcd121`. Registered in\n296: `opencode.json` as `mcp.servers[\"unsloth-studio\"]` → 23 MCP tools\n297: (`studio_status`, `load_model`, `chat`, `datasets`, `start_training`,\n298: `list_training_runs`, `export_model`, `get_job`, `cancel`, …). Shell fallback:\n299: `python3 tools/unsloth_studio.py <tool> '<json>'` (also `list`, `describe`,\n300: `@file` for big payloads). Studio's own python is\n301: `~/.unsloth/studio/unsloth_studio/bin/python` (the `.venv_t5_*` dirs are NOT\n302: venvs). The `unsloth` MCP server already in opencode.json is the community\n303: OtotaO one, not Studio.\n304: \n305: **The empty-content bug (do not re-derive).** LFM2.5's chat template opens\n306: `<think>` UNCONDITIONALLY — `add_generation_prompt` renders\n307: `<｜start▁of▁sentence｜><|Bot|>\\n<think>` with NO `enable_thinking` toggle, so that\n308: param cannot be used to suppress it. Studio's `ReasoningChannelNormalizer`\n309: splits output at `</think>`: before → reasoning_content, after → content. An SFT\n310: on think-less data (e.g. `no_robots`) teaches the model to answer immediately\n311: → it never closes the block → `content` is EMPTY and everything lands in\n312: `reasoning_content`. **Fix: training targets must contain a literal `</think>`\n313: BEFORE the answer.** The template's `keep_thinking` is true for the LAST\n314: assistant turn, so the `split(\"</think>\")[-1]` strip does not fire and the tag\n315: survives into training text — but it DOES fire for earlier turns, so keep\n316: rows