tudio\n346: dataset root — `~/.unsloth/studio/assets/datasets/` — so put big blends in\n347: `~/.unsloth/studio/assets/datasets/blends/`. This bypasses the ~3 MiB\n348: base64 upload cap entirely.\n349: \n350: **Studio has NO DPO/KTO/ORPO trainer** (grep over the whole backend → zero\n351: hits; `training_type` enum is `LoRA/QLoRA` | `Full Finetuning` | `Continued\n352: Pretraining`, and `worker.py:3035` refuses Continued Pretraining on MLX). So\n353: DPO datasets (prompt/chosen/rejected) can only be used by training on the\n354: **chosen** response. Same reason there is no `kto` in Studio's PIPELINES.\n355: \n356: **Studio's `datasets` is 4.3.0 → script datasets are DEAD** (no more\n357: `trust_remote_code` scripts). `piqa`, `natural-instructions`, `apps`,\n358: `lmsys-chat-1m`, `bbh`, `logiqa`, `cinematika` only exist via the\n359: `refs/convert/parquet` branch; `cinematika` also needs a pyarrow fallback\n360: because `datasets` chokes on its nested `list<struct<...>>`. Load order that\n361: works: main-branch raw JSONL → parquet branch → `load_dataset(repo, config)`\n362: → `load_dataset(repo)`.\n363: \n364: **Blended dataset (built 2026-10-22):** `tools/build_studio_blend_dataset.py`\n365: (persona payload + 45 Hub sources in 4 groups, per-source budgets, think-fix\n366: applied to every assistant turn, real-tokenizer 950-token cap, SHA1 dedupe,\n367: seed 3407) → `tools/decontaminate_studio_blend.py` (bge-small-en-v1.5 on CPU,\n368: cosine vs the repo's 20-benchmark battery, ~38 k items) → 16 632 rows → **16 541**\n369: clean. Only 91 dropped (0.55 %). **The 8-word-shingle guard is load-bearing:**\n370: MCQ train/test sets are stylistically identical, so a pure cosine threshold\n371: wipes out arc/winogrande/piqa/boolq. And `WORD_RE=[a-z0-9']+` finds NOTHING in\n372: CJK → every Chinese row normalised to `\"\"` and \"exactly matched\" the Chinese\n373: benchmarks (it nuked 432 of 599 HumanlikeRP rows) — `norm_key()` now returns\n374: None for text with no word characters.\n375: \n376: **Eval suite (pre-registered, `tools/studio_eval_suite.py`):** the probe set\n377: is fixed before scoring and is not selected by the metric it feeds. Classes:\n378: `format` (empty-content bug), `arithmetic` (POSITIVE CONTROL — 17×23 must be\n379: 391, not the parroted \"23\"), `persona`, `over_refusal` (benign-but-edgy, must\n380: NOT refuse), `under_refusal` (harmful, SHOULD refuse). Reports the refusal\n381: gap between the two sides. Two-sided scoring is mandatory: a model that\n382: answers everything and one that refuses everything both score 0 on the gap.\n383: \n384: **The think-fix is PROVEN (2026-10-22, control run\n385: `job_20261022_154129_691a2fb8`):** base content_nonempty_rate **0.143** vs\n386: think-fixed persona SFT **1.000**. The untuned base is *already* broken for\n387: chat (12/14 probes → `<EMPTY CONTENT, reasoning only>`) ⇒ the empty-content\n388: bug is a property of the **Heretic/JANG template**, not of any SFT.\n389: **arithmetic 0.25 and refuse_harmful 0.0 are IDENTICAL in base and SFT** ⇒\n390: they are inherited from the heretic + 2-bit-expert quant base, NOT caused by\n391: the SFT. The \"17×23 → 23\" parroting is a base-capability problem, so a\n392: better SFT cannot fix it — it needs the RL env or a stronger base.\n393: \n394: **`eval_split` ONLY works with a HUB dataset:** `eval_split` is read inside\n395: `_load_hf_train_and_eval_datasets`; the `local_datasets` path sets\n396: `eval_dataset = None` ALWAYS. So a local parquet can never report eval_loss\n397: (why the no_robots run had eval_loss NULL for all 3 168 steps). The blend is\n398: therefore trained from the Hub repo with an explicit `validation` split.\n399: `eval_steps` is an interval in OPTIMIZER STEPS, not a fraction. Valid split\n400: names: eval/validation/valid/val/test.\n401: \n402: **Published (public, per the user's explicit choice):\n403: `MC7ever/super-lfm-blend-v1`** — 16 540 rows, 9 852 499 B, **4 127 942\n404: tokens**; train 15 713 / validation 827 (stratified 5 % per source).\n405: Rebuild chain: `build_studio_blend_dataset.py` →\n406: `decontaminate_studio_blend.py` → `publish_blend_to_hf.py`.\n407: \n408: **Bench battery (`tools/studio_bench.py`):** the repo's 20 benchmarks scored\n409: through the Studio API. NOT lm-eval — the JANG base is U32-packed with no\n410: `quantization_config`, so transformers/unsloth cannot load it at all. NOT\n411: loglikelihood — Studio's completions schema has no `echo` field. So: ask for\n412: the LETTER, one generation per item, and RECORD the channel per probe\n413: (content vs reasoning_content) so \"wrong channel\" is distinguishable from\n414: \"wrong answer\". `--selftest` is a positive control (feeds each item's own\n415: gold answer back through the parser) and it caught 4 real item-builder bugs\n416: (sciq index order, truthful_qa labels are ints not strings, MMLU-ProX uses\n417: `option_0..9` + a letter `answer`, eq-bench uses `reference_answer`).\n418: \n419: **RL environment (`tools/rl/`, 8 files, 25 self-checks):** verifiers (SQL\n420: executes against a rebuilt in-memory SQLite and compares RESULT SETS; Python\n421: in a subprocess with a 10 s timeout; 17 format rules; persona rubric),\n422: task families, reward composition with penalties capped at 0.5, the rollout\n423: loop (tool call = a JSON object, results fed back as `[tool_result: ...]`),\n424: `profile.py` (reward profiling across models in capability order — the\n425: pre-flight step the Unsloth/NVIDIA guide insists on), and `grpo_export.py`\n426: (answer must NOT reveal the reasoning). **Two-sided refusal pairing:**\n427: benign/harmful tasks sharing a task_id stem score as a pair,\n428: reward = mean − 0.5·|gap| ⇒ a blanket-refuser and a blanket-answerer score\n429: the same and only a discriminator wins. A perfect family has ZERO variance\n430: and is useless to GRPO (group-relative advantage needs within-group spread)\n431: — that is the \"TOO EASY\" signal the profiler looks for.\n432: \n433: **DPO:** Studio has no DPO/ORPO/KTO trainer (a Studio limit, not an Unsloth\n434: one — `PatchDPOTrainer` works). And the **24B JANG base cannot be loaded by\n435: transformers** (U32-packed safetensors) ⇒ local DPO needs a standard bf16\n436: LFM2.5 (1.2B/2.6B/350M); the 24B DPO must run remotely on bf16 weights\n437: (`OS-Software/LFM2.5-24B-A2B-Uncensored-Heretic` ~372 GB → 1×H200 or 2×H100\n438: + host RAM). `tools/build_studio_pref_dataset.py` → `data/super_lfm/pref_v1.parquet`\n439: (14 310 pairs, 9 sources, think-fixed on chosen AND rejected, decontaminated\n440: against the same 20 benchmarks). `tools/train_dpo.py`: beta 0.1, **LR 5e-6**\n441: (the RL/DPO rate, NOT the 2e-4 for SFT), LoRA r16 α32, q/k/v/o/gate/up/down,\n442: effective batch 16. **Template adaptation:** the Heretic/JANG template opens\n443: `<think>` unconditionally so the completion must be `</think>{answer}`, but the\n444: OFFICIAL LiquidAI LFM2.5 templates do NOT open one, so the completion is just\n445: `{answer}` and the baked-in prefix must be stripped. Getting that wrong\n446: either emits a stray `</think>` or re-creates the empty-content bug.\n447: \n448: **Export disk hazard:** `core/export/export.py:1384` — on MLX, `export_merged_model`\n449: calls `save_pretrained_merged(save_method=\"merged_16bit\")`; the base is 186.2B\n450: params ⇒ **~372 GB** merge, and the export backend has NO disk-space guard.\n451: The pipeline exports `lora` first (~400 MB) then `gguf` Q4_K_M (~110 GB),\n452: skipping any format when free < need + 20 GB. `merged` is never attempted.\n453: \n454: ## Open queue\n455: 7-way soup (Pitcher) → evolve search → MoE-v2 graft on winner → RunPod\n456: training (never M5) → persona → quant (GGUF blocked: no spark2_5 in\n457: llama.cpp) → RIG benches winner-only (SWE/Terminal/OSWorld/GAIA/RP-judge).\n458: Studio-side (super lfm): the blend run `job_20261022_180225_afc24ca2`\n459: (16 540 rows v1, 2 epochs, lr 1e-4, 3 492 steps ≈ 8.4 h) is in flight →\n46