n.Linear layers\n2. Calls model.quantize() which converts nn.Linear to QuantizedLinear based on the config\n3. Loads the weights\n\nBut the weights in the safetensors are ALREADY quantized (they have .scales and .biases). So when `model.load_weights(weights)` is called, it loads the pre-quantized weights into the QuantizedLinear layers.\n\nWait, but there might be an issue. When `quantize_spark.py` ran `quantize_model`, it might have saved the model with `model.save_pretrained()` or similar, which saves the quantized weights. But the `quantize_model` function might not save the weights in the right format.\n\nLet me check what `quantize_spark.py` actually did. I don't have the file content anymore (it was compressed). Let me look at it.\n\nActually, let me just re-read the quantize_spark.py file.",
