re** (each determined independently per turn, each overridable by param):\n\n1. **Reasoning** (10 modes → native `none|low|high`, mapping exactly as your table — `extreme` stays on native `high` with the full creative-validation block, no invented fourth level)\n2. **Construct** (16, the session frame): all 15 originals + new **`ai_engineer`** (LLM/MLA/MoE/KV-cache/quantization/vLLM/llama.cpp/cloud GPU fleets — keyword-trips on \"llm\", \"mla\", \"kv cache\", \"vllm\", \"gpu cluster\"…)\n3. **Persona** (8, how it acts): joe, friend + new **`top_dawg`** (big-dog energy), **`griefer`** (chaos agent), **`anarchist`**, **`boy_kisser`**, plus the two influencer modes moved here (they were always voices)\n4. **Identity** (24, who it believes it is): all originals + new **twink, femboy, tomboy, futanari, kitty_boy, kitty_girl, dog_boy, dog_girl** (placed ahead of kemonomimi so \"catboy\"→kitty_boy while fox/animal-ears stay generic), **spy, imposter, hacker** (fiction-voiced — no operational real-harm tradecraft in the blocks), plus the two below\n\n**Two framings I chose deliberately, both hard-walled in the prompt text:**\n- **`age_regression`** — SFW-only comfort/caregiver \"little space\" mode; the block states the headspace is *never* sexual, all characters are adults, regression is a state not an age\n- **`lolita_fashion`** — the Lolita *fashion subculture* identity (gothic/classic/sweet, brand culture); the block states the fashion is non-sexual by community norm and the mode never carries sexual content\n\n**Minja fixes from your spec doc, all in:**\n- `\\n`/`\\t` replaces **dropped** and flagged in the header (keywords after a line break may miss — normalize at runtime); punctuation stripping kept\n- `loop.previtem/nextitem` **kept** for tool grouping, flagged as the known minja risk with the fallback spelled out\n- Header states native modes as `none | low | high`; `tojson` bare; string tool-args pass through verbatim (no `fromjson`); explicit **stateless — no en