on from listed models** | ❌ Not looked at | None of the HF links you pasted were reviewed. |\n\n## What the bigger probe showed\n\nYou ran 40 jobs and the output is clear — **the announce problem persists**:\n\n- Every dynamic-frame response narrates its choice in thinking: \"Construct: probably coder is most fitting…\", \"Frame: coder — senior engineer…\", \"Construct: coder fits — senior engineer, simplest correct runnable code…\"\n- Even with forced constructs like `construct=coder`, it still says \"Coder mode is forced. Simple, runnable, commented code.\"\n- With `effort=off` it's clean (just code, no meta) — but then personas/identities don't colour the voice at all.\n\nSo the template plumbing works, but the model hasn't learned silent inhabit yet. That requires training data + SFT.\n\n---\n\n## Your wishlist — honest read\n\n**GSQ / RCO / Pollard weights / Paretix / fit quants / rounded / auto round:** These are all quantization techniques that would need to be researched, implemented, and tested from scratch. None exist in the current pipeline. If you want to chase lower BPW (toward that 4.2 target), these are candidates to experiment with — but they're new work, not done.\n\n**Grab inspiration from the ~40 HF models you listed:** None have been reviewed. Some are Spark-X2.6-4B fine-tunes (Draftfit, SQL-Cypher-Agent, CED, EAGLE3, AgentFast, Blender, Radiance, etc.) and some are teacher models for synthetic data generation (DavidAU Qwen 27B/9B, Nemotron 74B/30B). If you want to:\n- Use a big teacher model to generate anti-announcement SFT data → the DavidAU/Nemotron links are relevant\n- Merge or adapt techniques from other Spark fine-tunes → those would need individual review\n\n**Eliminate weird nuances and noise:** This maps to the Gentle-Coding graft already in the template (soft validation, human voice, no sycophancy/hedging, \"to the point\"). The template has it; the model doesn't obey it yet because it hasn't been trained on data that rewards that behavior.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended next steps (pick one)\n\n1. **Build anti-announcement SFT data** — Use a big teacher model (one of the DavidAU Qwen or Nemotron links) to generate examples where the answer silently inhabits a frame with no announcement, plus private `[frame: …]` tags in thinking. Expand `make_synth.py` beyond its current 9 seeds.\n\n2. **Unsloth SFT** — Train on that data with the same `chat_template.jinja` so silent inhabit sticks.\n\n3. **Chase lower BPW** — Research/implement one of GSQ, auto-round, etc. to get from 5.9 → 4.2 BPW.\n\n4. **Review the listed HF models** — Pick a few that look useful and see what techniques they use that could be ported in.\n\nWhich direction do you want to go?"
