ance \"Acceptance\")\n\n  - [Use](#use \"Use\")\n\n# [](#spark-x26-4b-dspark-draft) Spark-X2.6-4B DSpark Draft\n\nThis model is part of the validation set for [Draftfit](https://github.com/JayYun98/Draftfit), a platform for building, converting and evaluating speculative decoding drafts with shared target features.\n\nA DSpark draft for [Spark-X2.6-4B](https://huggingface.co/XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B). It requires the target model for text generation.\n\n## [](#acceptance) Acceptance\n\n| Evaluation | Official draft | This draft |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Development | 37\\.93% | **40\\.11%** |\n| Confirmation | 35\\.85% | **38\\.44%** |\n\nMeasured with the same greedy PyTorch prefix verifier, seven draft proposals, 64 output tokens and 24 prompts per partition. Acceptance is accepted/proposed draft tokens, excluding target bonus tokens. All outputs match the target exactly.\n\nThese small internal benchmarks had prior evaluation exposure. Both paired prompt bootstrap 95% intervals include zero. Production serving speed and full original C++ runtime parity are unverified.\n\n## [](#use) Use\n\nLoad `model.safetensors` into the included `SparkDSpark(official_config())` reference with `safetensors.torch.load_file`. A compatible Draftfit Spark target adapter is required; provenance is in `experiment-manifest.json`. This is a custom reference checkpoint, not a drop-in vLLM, SGLang or MLX model.\n\n**Downloads last month**\n: \\-\n\nSafetensors[](https://huggingface.co/docs/safetensors)\n\nModel size\n\n0\\.6B params\n\nTensor type\n\nF32\n\n·\n\nBF16\n\n·\n\nFiles info\n\nInference Providers [NEW](https://huggingface.co/docs/inference-providers)\n\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. [🙋 Ask for provider support](/spaces/huggingface/InferenceSupport/discussions/new?title=jayyun98/Spark-X2.6-4B-Draftfit-DSpark-Autoresearch&description=React%20to%20this%20comment%20with%20an%20emoji%20to%20vote%20for%20%5Bjayyun98%2FSpark-X2.6-4B-Draftfit-DSpark-Autoresearch%5