-calling agent. 94,745 examples (~66M tokens), 1 epoch: 90,549 gold calls + 4,196 self-generated traces (only kept if query passed execution checks). LoRA rank 16/alpha 32/dropout 0.05, AdamW lr 1e-4, 3% warmup, cosine decay, batch 32, max len 4096. Checkpoint at step 1,500 of 2,961. +10.7 points execution accuracy overall (32.5%→43.7%). Datasets: trl-lab/SQaLe-2-text-to-SQL-Queries, gretelai/synthetic_text_to_sql, neo4j/text2cypher-2025v1, megagonlabs/cypherbench. Thinking budget 1024 tokens.\n\n5. **CED** (darioooooo0o) — Causal Encoder-Decoder split retrofit from DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash paper (arXiv 2609.19969). Split at layer 24 (v2 recommended; v1 at layer 18 lost long-context retrieval). Layers 0-23 = encoder (original weights), 24-35 = decoder whose 3 global layers read K/V projected from RMSNorm(H_24). Closed-form ridge-regression init of 6 K/V projections from ~0.5M tokens PG19/code/chat/synthetic retrieval. + LoRA distillation on decoder + encoder layers 14-17. Prefill 1.5-2x speedup, decode unchanged. KL to original ~0.089 (comparable to IQ4_XS-IQ3_M quant). Saves prefill compute, not memory.\n\n6. **EAGLE-3** (VitreousCut) — One-layer EAGLE-3 draft head (218M params) for Spark-X2.6-4B. Trained on 21.96M tokens: 10M codeparrot-clean Python, 3M Magicoder instruction→code, 2M WikiText-103 prose, 7M UltraChat-200k conversation. Objective: CE against target's own argmax + 0.5*MSE on fed-back prenorm state + depth-1 CE from training-time test. Key insight: relabel on verifier argmax (not corpus token) lifted prose acceptance 0.49→0.81. Training-time test (feed own output back as input) raised depth-1 acceptance 0.50→0.70. ~2.57x throughput on CPU target + GPU head placement.\n\n7. **Therapy-EfficientThink-SFT** (denjhang) — Spark-X2.5-4B, LoRA r32, 56 samples, 3 epoch, teacher Qwen3.8-Flash-Next 125B. 19 real agent session replays: 12/19 cured (heavy 566s/32K/zero-output cases → 4-25s), avg turn 249s→67s (3.7x), dirty context+image 2.2s tool call. BUT long task planning (write plane game) still deadlocks (8-10min zero output). Root cause: training sequences limited to 3K tokens (Windows TDR watchdog), so longest samples never entered training. Next step: TdrDelay unlock 8K sequences + DPO preference pairs.\n\n8. **BetterWright-4b** (ProCreations) — Full-parameter SFT of Spark-X2.5-4B for browser agent (Playwright). FlexAttention sliding-window block masks, stochastic-rounding 8-bit AdamW (torchao), gradient checkpointing, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 96GB. 502 execution-verified BetterWright exec trajectories (teachers: DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731, Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B, Kimi-K2.6, GLM-5.3-Flash, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next), kept only when strict LLM judge scored ≥7/10. Per-turn reasoning rewritten into compact rationales (15-120 words). 2182 sequences (33.4M tokens, 5.38M supervised tokens, max 97,693 tokens), 898 general-assistant replay samples. 122 steps, peak LR 8e-6, 20 warmup, cosine decay to 10%. Results: judge mean score 1.21→2.40, grounded answers 22%→40%, reasoning tokens/task 11,495→3,140 (-73%), output tokens/task 21,067→14,810 (-30%), browser steps/task 60.9→37.1 (-40%). Recommended serving window 262,144 tokens.\n\n9. **SparkMuse-4B** (hcnote) — Creative writing/novel-generation/roleplay, NSFW, 1M context (model card hidden behind sensitive-content gate).\n\n10. **Spark-X2.5-4B-Writing-EP1** (hcnote) — Creative writing/novel/roleplay, NSFW (model card hidden behind sensitive-content gate).\n\nNOT YET FETCHED (title/tags only): darioooooo0o/spark-4b-engram, sriq-ai/sriq-spark-v1.4, Takenoko12345678/Spark-X2.5-4B-Japanese, webmp3/Sakura-Spark-X2.5-4B-GGUF, JamieBradfield/Spark-X2.6-4B-AgentFast, ZZRI/Feihua-n2-1.7B-preview/n1/n2, rizzoaiacademy/rizzo-flow-1.7b, ApollonLabs/Heliactis-1-4B, Takenoko12345678/Spark-X2.5-4B-Japanese-Pitcher, Lalakai/Hunter-1-1.7B, win10/Spark-engram-4B-V2, win10/spark-temporal-engram-4b-v3, win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1, hotocooo/Spark-X2.6-4B-Blender, gostar77/spark-x2.6-4b-radiance, iceair32