riq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6/viewer/default/train)\n\n---\n\n- [ Previous]()\n\n- [1](/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6/viewer/default/train?p=0)\n\n- [2](/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6/viewer/default/train?p=1)\n\n- [3](/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6/viewer/default/train?p=2)\n\n- [...](#)\n\n- [100](/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6/viewer/default/train?p=99)\n\n- [Next](/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6/viewer/default/train?p=1)\n\n- [What v1.6 adds](#what-v16-adds \"What v1.6 adds\")\n\n  - [Verification that catches something](#verification-that-catches-something \"Verification that catches something\")\n\n  - [Difficulty, and traces that scale with it](#difficulty-and-traces-that-scale-with-it \"Difficulty, and traces that scale with it\")\n\n  - [Harness prompts on half the corpus](#harness-prompts-on-half-the-corpus \"Harness prompts on half the corpus\")\n\n- [Composition](#composition \"Composition\")\n\n- [Token statistics](#token-statistics \"Token statistics\")\n\n- [Load](#load \"Load\")\n\n- [Format for Qwen3.8 training](#format-for-qwen38-training \"Format for Qwen3.8 training\")\n\n- [Notes](#notes \"Notes\")\n\n- [Provenance](#provenance \"Provenance\")\n\n  - [Release chain](#release-chain \"Release chain\")\n\n- [License](#license \"License\")\n\n# [](#sriq-sft-v16) sriq-sft-v1.6\n\nShareGPT-compatible supervised fine-tuning conversations by [SRIQ](https://sriq.org). Questions are generated in 30 languages. Assistant targets contain compressed Simplified Chinese reasoning followed by the original final answer. The final answer is not rewritten by the compression step.\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Rows** | 9,988 |\n| **Languages** | 30 |\n| **Turns** | system, human, gpt |\n| **Reasoning** | compressed Simplified Chinese inside `<think>` tags |\n| **Verification** | 19\\.5% of traces catch a real mistake and repair it |\n| **Difficulty** | easy / medium / hard, with trace length scaled to match |\n| **Previous version** | [sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.5](https://huggingface.co/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.5) |\n\n- `conversations`: a system turn, a human turn, then one GPT turn.\n\n- System turn: `from` is `system`; `value` contains either a short generic preamble or a long synthetic coding-harness preamble.\n\n- Human turn: `from` is `human`; `value` contains the question.\n\n- GPT turn: `from` is `gpt`; `value` contains `<think>Chinese reasoning</think>` followed by the final answer.\n\n- Extra columns: `topic`, `difficulty`, `language` (the requested question language), and `verification` (new in v1.6).\n\nThere are no rejected responses in the SFT export.\n\n## [](#what-v16-adds) What v1.6 adds\n\n### [](#verification-that-catches-something) Verification that catches something\n\nThrough v1.5 the verification step could only ever agree with itself. The compressed trace is rewritten from a chain of thought that already produced the final answer, so the check at the end had nothing to find: **0\\.9%** of v1.5 traces caught a mistake, and 546 closed on an explicit 答案对. A model trained on that learns the shape of checking without the function — the first adapter trained on v1.5 reached the right answer on IMO 1990 P3 through steps containing `p | p-1`, which holds for no prime, and stamped it correct.\n\nA share of v1.6 rows are generated down a second path: one step of the reasoning is deliberately wrong, and the verification catches it, names it and redoes it. The final answer is the original correct one either way.\n\n| `verification` | Rows | Share |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `correct` — the check found a real mistake and repaired it | 1,951 | **19\\.5%** |\n| `confirm` — the check ran and found nothing | 8,037 | 80\\.5% |\n\nA row is rejected and regenerated unless the planted mistake appears verbatim in the trace, and unless the trace stops short of announcing it before the check. A trace that merely claims to have verified something is the thing being fixed.\n\n### [](#difficulty-and-traces-that-scale-with-it) Difficulty, and traces that scale with it\n\nEvery row in v1.3 through v1.5 was `difficulty: hard`, so nothing in the corpus taught a model that a cheap question deserves a cheap answer. v1.6 samples all three and gives the compression step a length budget per difficulty.\n\n| Difficulty | Rows | Median reasoning tokens |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| easy | 1,872 | **25** |\n| medium | 2,648 | 140 |\n| hard | 5,468 | 254 |\n\nFor comparison, v1.5 spent a median of 349 reasoning tokens on everything, because everything was hard. An easy question in v1.6 costs about a fourteenth of that.\n\n### [](#harness-prompts-on-half-the-corpus) Harness prompts on half the corpus\n\nModels fine-tuned on a corpus of short system prompts hold Chinese reasoning under a short system prompt, and drift back to English behind a real agent harness. Half of v1.6 carries a synthetic coding-harness preamble — persona line, guidelines, a `# Skills` listing, project context, an environment footer — so the behaviour is trained where it otherwise collapses.\n\n| System prompt | Rows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `You are a helpful assistant` | 4,988 |\n| Synthetic coding-harness preamble | 5,000 |\n\nHarness preambles run to a median of 1,005 tokens and a maximum of 1,933. The user turn is still an ordinary question, not a tool-call trace: the preamble is distractor context, and the target is that the model keeps reasoning in Chinese and answering in the question's language despite it.\n\n## [](#composition) Composition\n\n| Axis | Split |\n| --- | --- |\n| Topic | math 6,081 (60.9%) · coding 3,907 (39.1%) |\n| Difficulty | hard 5,468 · medium 2,648 · easy 1,872 |\n| Verification | confirm 8,037 · correct 1,951 |\n| Languages | 30, between 295 and 390 rows each |\n\nArabic, Bengali, Czech, Dutch, English, French, German, Greek, Hebrew, Hindi, Indonesian, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Persian, Polish, Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Spanish, Swahili, Swedish, Tamil, Thai, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, Ukrainian, Urdu, Vietnamese.\n\n## [](#token-statistics) Token statistics\n\nCounts use `tiktoken` `cl100k_base`, not the training model's tokenizer.\n\n| Slice | Total tokens |\n| --- | --- |\n| System prompts | 5,192,983 |\n| Reasoning | 2,312,789 |\n| Final answer | 13,082,224 |\n| Reasoning \\+ final answer, including think tags | 15,445,506 |\n\n## [](#load) Load\n\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\n\ndataset = load_dataset(\"sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6\", split=\"train\")\nconversation = dataset[0][\"conversations\"]\n```\n\n## [](#format-for-qwen38-training) Format for Qwen3.8 training\n\nThe export uses standard ShareGPT fields. Qwen3.8's native template expects reasoning in a separate field, so convert the record before applying that template:\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer\n\nsystem, question = conversation[0][\"value\"], conversation[1][\"value\"]\nresponse = conversation[2][\"value\"]\nreasoning, answer = response.removeprefix(\"<think>\").split(\"</think>\", 1)\nmessages = [\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": question},\n    {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"reasoning_content\": reasoning, \"content\": answer.strip()},\n]\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B\")\ntext = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n    messages,\n    tokenize=False,\n    add_generation_prompt=False,\n    preserve_thinking=True,\n)\n```\n\nFor other models, adapt the ShareGPT roles and fields to the trainer's expected conversation schema while retaining the complete GPT `value`. Do not place the same reasoning in both `content` and `reasoning_content` for Qwen's template.\n\nFor SFT, include the assistant's reasoning and final answer in the loss and mask system/user/prompt tokens. Check that the rendered training text retains the Chinese reasoning and that the assistant loss mask covers it. Use the target tokenizer to check lengths and keep repeated questions in the same train/evaluation split.\n\nThe harness rows are long. Set the sequence length to keep them whole — truncating the preamble removes the signal those rows exist to teach. If you must cap, drop the row rather than truncate it.\n\n## [](#notes) Notes\n\n`verification` is a new column, so this dataset cannot be appended to a v1.5 repository; the schemas differ.\n\nNothing here is a benchmark result. The figures describe what the corpus contains, not measured gains from training on it.\n\n## [](#provenance) Provenance\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Data revision** | `fa9e48709631a7be4eae3e38252c3a26fff3c0f3` |\n| **Published** | 2026-09-20 22:31 UTC |\n| **Built with** | pipeline commit `661ca90` in [`sriq/sriq-sft`](https://git.nixre.dev/git/sriq/sriq-sft) |\n| **Previous** | [v1.5](https://huggingface.co/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.5) |\n| **Trained into** | [sriq-diffusiongemma-26B-A4B-v1.6](https://huggingface.co/sriq-ai/sriq-diffusiongemma-26B-A4B-v1.6) |\n\nThe card above may change; the parquet at that revision will not. Pin it when training, so the corpus is the one that was measured:\n\n```python\nload_dataset(\"sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6\", split=\"train\",\n             revision=\"fa9e48709631a7be4eae3e38252c3a26fff3c0f3\")\n```\n\n### [](#release-chain) Release chain\n\nEach version exists to close a defect in the one before it.\n\n| Version | Rows | Data revision | What it introduced | The defect it left behind |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v1.3 | 2,703 | `84f74b6` | compressed Simplified Chinese reasoning, 30 languages | traces stop at the answer — 15\\.2% carry a `验` block, 0\\.3% end on an explicit judgement |\n| v1.4 | 825 | `be3a4b6` | a verification step closing the trace (95.4% carry `验`) | Chinese reasoning reverts to English behind a long agent-harness prompt |\n| v1.5 | 1,424 | `e7ee870` | long synthetic harness preambles on 599 of 1,424 rows | the check inherited from v1.4 could only ever agree — 0\\.9% caught a mistake |\n| **v1.6** | 9,988 | `fa9e487` | verification that catches a real planted mistake (19.5%), graded difficulty, a `verification` column | — current release |\n\nThe commits behind this release:\n\n| Commit | What it changed |\n| --- | --- |\n| `5d05bed` | the self-check generation path — one step deliberately wrong, the verification catches it |\n| `56d3517` | moved the compression prompts out of Python into `prompts/*.txt` |\n| `2a83270` | the prompt shows the target register as a worked before/after instead of describing it |\n| `b782b8f` | rejects rows that telegraph the planted mistake before the check; scales trace length to difficulty |\n| `759216c` | support for endpoints that cannot constrain decoding (no dataset effect) |\n| `661ca90` | compression measured on the trace rather than the whole response |\n\nOne more difference from v1.5, not attributable to a single commit: harness preambles here run to a median of 1,005 and a maximum of 1,933 tokens, against v1.5's median 1,518 and maximum 15,976, so the harness rows now fit inside a practical context cap.\n\n**The corpus is ordered, not shuffled.** Rows 0–4,987 carry the generic preamble and rows 4,988–9,987 carry the harness preamble, the same layout v1.5 had. A tail split therefore holds out nothing but harness rows, and a head split trains on none of them. Shuffle before splitting.\n\n## [](#license) License\n\nApache-2.0.\n\nCopy to bucket\n\nUse this dataset\n\n**Downloads last month**\n\n: 74\n\n[]()\n\nNumber of rows:\n\n9,988\n\n[]()\n\nTotal file size:\n\n83\\.3 MB\n\n## Models trained or fine-tuned on sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6\n\n[](/sriq-ai/SRIQ-MiniCPM5-2B-v1.6)\n\n![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/69ccfe9d66dc2f65a558e917/MoYpZKNeScPZHJffQc2UO.png)\n\n#### sriq-ai/SRIQ-MiniCPM5-2B-v1.6\n\nText Generation • 3B • Updated Sep 26 • 269 • 1\n\n[](/sriq-ai/sriq-diffusiongemma-26B-A4B-v1.6)\n\n![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/69ccfe9d66dc2f65a558e917/MoYpZKNeScPZHJffQc2UO.png)\n\n#### sriq-a