 [Contents](#contents \"Contents\")\n\n- [Fields](#fields \"Fields\")\n\n- [How it was built](#how-it-was-built \"How it was built\")\n\n# [](#sriq-svg-flow-v10) sriq-svg-flow-v1.0\n\nThe **workflow** of the SVG pipeline, by [SRIQ](https://sriq.org): every message of the tool loop that draws an image as SVG, in OpenAI chat format. One row per conversation: the draft, the refinement, the request, and the reasoning trace.\n\nPipeline: [https://git.nixre.dev/sriq/svg-distill](https://git.nixre.dev/sriq/svg-distill) (Apache-2.0).\n\nThis is the agentic half of the corpus: the model sees the target image, calls tools to measure it, and edits the SVG until the render matches. It teaches the *procedure*, not the answer.\n\n> **Growing dataset.** This repo will keep growing: new rows are added and existing ones updated over time. Row counts below describe the current upload; pin a `revision` in `load_dataset` for a fixed snapshot.\n\n## [](#contents) Contents\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Rows** | 734 conversations |\n| **Turns** | system, user, assistant (with `tool_calls`), tool results |\n| **Images** | 9,968 files under `images/`, referenced from the messages as `images/<2 hex>/<hash>.png` |\n| **Messages** | 30,804 |\n| **Conversations** | 120 draft1, 118 prompt, 120 refine, 125 trace\\_img+text2svg, 127 trace\\_img2svg, 124 trace\\_text2svg |\n\n## [](#fields) Fields\n\n- `messages`: the conversation as it was sent, in OpenAI chat format. Tool calls, tool results and reasoning are kept; the inline images are replaced by files under `images/`.\n\n- `tools`: the tool schemas the model could call (`read_svg`, `edit_svg`, `sample_target`, `trace_region`, `zoom`).\n\n- `conv`: which conversation it is (`draft1`, `refine`, `prompt`, `trace_text2svg`, `trace_img2svg`, `trace_img+text2svg`).\n\n- `model`: the model that produced it. `source`: the target image. `url`: where that image came from. `run`: the run id.\n\n## [](#how-it-was-built) How it was built\n\n1. **Target.** A photo flattened into a simple flat-color version by an image-edit model.\n\n2. **Draft.** A vision model writes a complete SVG from the target.\n\n3. **Refine.** The same model improves it through tools: exact colors (`sample_target`), exact outlines (`trace_region`), close-ups (`zoom`). Every edit is scored against the target and reverted when it does not help. A text-only review then lists what is still wrong, and the model gets a budget of tool calls to fix it.\n\n4. **Request and trace.** A second model writes the request that would ask for the drawing; a third writes the reasoning trace from the finished SVG.\n\nNothing here is a benchmark result.\n\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\nds = load_dataset(\"sriq-ai/sriq-svg-flow-v1.0\", split=\"train\")\n```\n\nCopy to bucket\n\nUse this dataset\n\n**Downloads last month**\n\n: 36\n\n[]()\n\nNumber of rows:\n\n734\n\n[]()\n\nTotal file size:\n\n1\\.2 GB\n\nSystem theme\n\nCompany\n\n[TOS](/terms-of-service) [Privacy](/privacy) [About](/huggingface) [Careers](https://apply.workable.com/huggingface/) [](/)\n\nWebsite\n\n[Models](/models) [Datasets](/datasets) [Spaces](/spaces) [Pricing](/pricing) [Docs](/docs)"
