d_dataset` for a fixed snapshot.\n\n## [](#contents) Contents\n\n|  | Rows | Request | Answer | Median trace tokens | Median answer chars |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| text2svg | 118 | a synthetic request | one SVG file | 2,335.5 | 7,223.0 |\n| img2svg | 118 | the photo (as an `images` column) \\+ one instruction | one SVG file |  |  |\n| img+text2svg | 118 | the photo \\+ the synthetic request | one SVG file |  |  |\n| **Total** | **354** |  |  |  |  |\n\nDifficulty over all rows: 24 easy / 117 medium / 213 hard. 118 images, each exported as three records (the request alone, the photo alone, both). Token counts use `cl100k_base`. Median render-vs-target similarity of the drawings: 0\\.967.\n\n## [](#fields) Fields\n\n- `conversations`: system (`You are a helpful assistant`), human (the request), gpt (`<think>trace</think>` \\+ the SVG).\n\n- `images`: the photo of the image records, as bytes; empty for the text-only records.\n\n- `topic`: always `svg`. `language`: always `English` (the request language). `verification`: always `confirm` (every trace checks the drawing it describes; no planted mistakes in this set).\n\n- `difficulty`: the number of elements the drawing uses (easy \\< 30, medium \\< 55, hard \\>= 55).\n\n- `source`: the target image the drawing came from. `score`: the similarity of the render to that target.\n\nThe two extra columns (`source`, `score`) and `images` are new against [sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6](https://huggingface.co/datasets/sriq-ai/sriq-sft-v1.6); select the shared columns to concatenate with it.\n\n## [](#how-it-was-built) How it was built\n\n1. **Target.** A photo is flattened by an image-edit model into a simple flat-color version, and that is the drawing the model has to reproduce.\n\n2. **Drawing.** A vision model drafts an SVG, then improves it through tools (`read_svg`, `edit_svg`, `sample_target`, `trace_region`, `zoom`): exact colors and outlines instead of guesses. Every edit is scored against the target and reverted when it does not help, so the source is always the best one.\n\n3. **Request.** A second model sees the finished SVG and its render and writes the request that would ask for it. The image records show the original photo with one of 30 instructions, or with a short reference line plus that request.\n\n4. **Trace.** A separate call writes the reasoning from the finished SVG, in the SRIQ register: telegraphic Simplified Chinese, working notes, closing with a `验：` check. The gate rejects a trace without a `验：` that shows its arithmetic, a trace that is not mostly Chinese, one with pasted markup or refusal text, one that does not quote numbers of this SVG, and a `验：` that names no element of the SVG. A rejected trace is retried in place, not the whole row.\n\n353 of 354 rows carry a trace; the rest export the SVG without one.\n\nEvery trace contains a `验：` (check) step. Nothing here is a benchmark result.\n\nTrain on the gpt turn (reasoning \\+ answer); mask system and human.\n\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\nds = load_dataset(\"sriq-ai/sriq-svg-sft-v1.0\", split=\"train\")\n```\n\nCopy to bucket\n\nUse this dataset\n\n**Downloads last month**\n\n: 41\n\n[]()\n\nNumber of rows:\n\n354\n\n[]()\n\nTotal file size:\n\n249 MB\n\nSystem theme\n\nCompany\n\n[TOS](/terms-of-service) [Privacy](/privacy) [About](/huggingface) [Careers](https://apply.workable.com/huggingface/) [](/)\n\nWebsite\n\n[Models](/models) [Datasets](/datasets) [Spaces](/spaces) [Pricing](/pricing) [Docs](/docs)"
