                "text": "[![Hugging Face's logo](/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face](/)\n\n- [ Models](/models)\n\n- [ Datasets](/datasets)\n\n- [ Spaces](/spaces)\n\n- [ Buckets](/storage)\n\n- [ Docs](/docs)\n\n- [ Enterprise](/enterprise)\n\n- [Pricing](/pricing)\n\n-\n\n  -\n\n    Website\n\n    - [ Tasks](/tasks)\n\n    - [ HuggingChat](/chat)\n\n    - [ Collections](/collections)\n\n    - [ Languages](/languages)\n\n    - [ Organizations](/organizations)\n\n  -\n\n    Community\n\n    - [ Blog](/blog)\n\n    - [ Posts](/posts)\n\n    - [ Daily Papers](/papers)\n\n    - [ Hardware](/hardware)\n\n    - [ Learn](/learn)\n\n    - [ Discord](/join/discord)\n\n    - [ Forum](https://discuss.huggingface.co/)\n\n    - [ GitHub](https://github.com/huggingface)\n\n  -\n\n    Solutions\n\n    - [ Team & Enterprise](/enterprise)\n\n    - [ Hugging Face PRO](/pro)\n\n    - [ Enterprise Support](/support)\n\n    - [ Inference Providers](/inference/models)\n\n    - [ Inference Endpoints](/inference-endpoints)\n\n    - [ Storage Buckets](/storage)\n\n-\n\n  ---\n\n- [Log In](/login)\n\n- [Sign Up](/join)\n\n#\n\n[](/win10)\n\n![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/640720285e6d06cc2cf346e4/p-U1ON7ZPNntBAnOo8FCE.png)\n\n[win10](/win10)\n\n/\n\n[spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1](/win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1)\n\nLike 0\n\n[](/models?library=safetensors)\n\nSafetensors\n\n[](/models?other=spark2_5)\n\nspark2\\_5\n\n[](/models?other=custom_code)\n\ncustom\\_code\n\n[ Model card](/win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1) [ Files Files and versions](/win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1/tree/main)\n\nxet\n\n[ Community](/win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1/discussions)\n\nCopy to bucket\n\n**YAML Metadata Warning:**empty or missing yaml metadata in repo card\n\nCheck out the [documentation](https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/model-cards#model-card-metadata) for more information.\n\n- [Spark-X2.5-4B V6](#spark-x25-4b-v6 \"Spark-X2.5-4B V6\")\n\n  - [Native serialization and sources](#native-serialization-and-sources \"Native serialization and sources\")\n\n  - [Training](#training \"Training\")\n\n  - [Supported-format regression](#supported-format-regression \"Supported-format regression\")\n\n  - [Loading](#loading \"Loading\")\n\n# [](#spark-x25-4b-v6) Spark-X2.5-4B V6\n\nA fresh original-backbone initialization of `belief_v6`, including the V6 beam engine. No previous trained model, adapter, or fitted codec was loaded. The ordinary Transformers generation entry point is inherited. The V3 date/event pathway is disabled.\n\nComplete weights contain a BF16 backbone and FP32 floating Engram parameters; LoRA has been merged. This export passed the predeclared supported-format regression gate and GPU clean-load, greedy, and beam checks. It is published as the official V6 replacement on the Hugging Face Hub.\n\n## [](#native-serialization-and-sources) Native serialization and sources\n\nLLaMA-Factory template: `spark2_5_tool`. The original tokenizer Jinja is preserved. System definitions use `## Tools` and `<tools>`; calls use `<tool_call>name<arg_key>key</arg_key><arg_value>value</arg_value></tool_call>`; results use `<|Tool|><tool_response>...</tool_response>`. Reasoning uses `<think>...</think>`.\n\nAll four registered sources were rebuilt as explicit native frames. Every original tool-result string was preserved; no conversation text or tool definitions were invented. Eight full-record previews matched the original Jinja token IDs. Original prose and code mentioning `function_call` or `observation` remain unchanged; zero residual roles are measured from parsed message fields. The registered Claude source has only user/assistant messages and no tool-result roles.\n\n| Source | Records | Original results | Native response wrappers | Legacy function\\_call/observation roles |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| claude\\_opus\\_4\\_7\\_traceinversion\\_qwen35 | 4761 | 0 | 0 | 0/0 |\n| ox\\_alpha\\_pi\\_traces\\_qwen35 | 936 | 13153 | 13153 | 0/0 |\n| fable5\\_cursor\\_traces\\_qwen35 | 233 | 19139 | 19139 | 0/0 |\n| lambda\\_hermes\\_agent\\_reasoning\\_qwen35 | 14691 | 132405 | 132405 | 0/0 |\n\nSource inconsistencies, including undefined function names and malformed typed arguments, are preserved rather than guessed or repaired. Nested XML in tool argument code is retained. Before/after samples, source paths and data audit evidence accompany the export.\n\n## [](#training) Training\n\nLLaMA-Factory, learning rate 0\\.0004, 64 optimizer steps, cutoff 512, batch 1, accumulation 2, LoRA rank 16/alpha 32, CUDA BF16 AMP, FP32 Bayesian mixture, disabled AMP weight cache, and nonreentrant activation checkpoints. Engram/belief parameters are in the optimizer; the newly fitted codec is frozen. Seed 2026101407; cosine schedule with four warmup steps. Checkpoints retain optimizer, scheduler and RNG state every eight steps.\n\nThe prepared set has 128 windows per source. Balanced sampling consumes 32 windows per source in the fixed run. Plain-source windows use LF's first-pair cutoff. Tool-source windows are contiguous full result/call pairs selected from the native LF stream, retaining the complete result and following assistant call within 512 tokens. Earlier history and the initial system frame lie outside these later windows; the full mapped corpora retain them. Query-group holdouts are excluded from training and codec fitting. This finite budget is not a full corpus epoch.\n\nCodec fitting uses only the new training windows from the four sources, with 256 continuous and 256 quantized steps. Reconstruction accuracy is 0\\.0, raw future NLL is 11\\.735454, and active codes per slot are \\[128, 128, 128, 128\\]. These weak reconstruction diagnostics do not establish semantic memory accuracy. Full metrics are in `evidence/codec-fit.json`.\n\nFirst logged objective 21\\.333708, last 10\\.572448, mean microbatch objective 14\\.921099. This objective combines language and V6 auxiliary losses. Peak allocated GPU memory: 13\\.617 GB; limit 80 GB. Stateful prepares execute once per labeled forward and are not repeated during checkpoint backward replay.\n\n## [](#supported-format-regression) Supported-format regression\n\nThe fixed set has eight semantic questions, two thinking modes and three interfaces, for 48 requests per model. OpenAI-shaped tools chat requests and directly serialized native tagged completions share identical prompt token IDs and use the same backend and generation configuration. They are paired entry paths, not independent semantic tests. Greedy decoding allows 1024 new tokens; no adaptive retries or missing-case exclusions. This is a controlled Transformers HTTP evaluator, not a SGLang deployment test.\n\nThe adoption gate requires both syntax-valid and exact typed-call counts to be at least the original baseline for each supported interface. Text JSON is reference only. These questions have been exposed in prior regression runs and are not an independent generalization benchmark.\n\n| Interface | Original exact calls | V6 exact calls |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| openai\\_tools | 16/16 | 16/16 |\n| native\\_tags | 16/16 | 16/16 |\n| text\\_json | 11/16 | 0/16 |\n\nSee [every case](/win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1/blob/main/tool-regression.md) and raw evidence for prompts, outputs and errors. Original loading required a runtime-only Transformers 5 tied-weight declaration adjustment; original source files and weights were unchanged.\n\n## [](#loading) Loading\n\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\npath = \"Spark-X2.5-4B-v6-lr4e4\"\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(path, trust_remote_code=True)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(path, trust_remote_code=True,\n    dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"cuda\").eval()\ninputs = tokenizer.apply_chat_template([{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What is 2 + 2?\"}],\n    add_generation_prompt=True, enable_thinking=False,\n    return_dict=False, return_tensors=\"pt\").cuda()\nwith torch.inference_mode():\n    output = model.generate(inputs, max_new_tokens=128, do_sample=False)\nprint(tokenizer.decode(output[0, inputs.shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=False))\n# Pass num_beams=4 for beam generation.\n```\n\nWeight size: 8,473,775,373 bytes. The original model license is retained. The user handles publication of the accepted local export.\n\n**Downloads last month**\n: 262\n\nSafetensors[](https://huggingface.co/docs/safetensors)\n\nModel size\n\n4B params\n\nTensor type\n\nF32\n\n·\n\nBF16\n\n·\n\nU8\n\n·\n\nChat template\n\nFiles info\n\nInference Providers [NEW](https://huggingface.co/docs/inference-providers)\n\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. [🙋 Ask for provider support](/spaces/huggingface/InferenceSupport/discussions/new?title=win10/spark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1&description=React%20to%20this%20comment%20with%20an%20emoji%20to%20vote%20for%20%5Bwin10%2Fspark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1%5D\\(%2Fwin10%2Fspark-predictive-belief-engram-4b-v1\\)%20to%20be%20supported%20by%20Inference%20Providers.%0A%0A\\(optional\\)%20Which%20providers%20are%20you%20interested%20in%3F%20\\(Novita%2C%20Hyperbolic%2C%20Together%E2%80%A6\\)%0A)\n\nSystem theme\n\nCompany\n\n[TOS](/terms-of-service) [Privacy](/privacy) [About](/huggingface) [Careers](https://apply.workable.com/huggingface/) [](/)\n\nWebsite\n\n[Models](/models) [Datasets](/datasets) [Spaces](/spaces) [Pricing](/pricing) [Docs](/docs)"
